; Tutorial_9_Conclusion.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=9 - Conclusion
Intro=What to carry away, and where to begin.
Setup=BatCon is installed and your reader is running.
Homework=Begin with a folder you convert often.

[step]
Say=Four things to carry away. One: Alt plus Control plus B opens BatCon.
Key=Alt+Control+B
Hear=BatCon dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit

[step]
Say=Two: every format BatCon can make is listed, and a source that cannot become it is skipped, with the reason.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Target format: list box
Hear=Markdown document (md)

[step]
Say=Three: your files are safe. A result appears only when its conversion works, and a source is never overwritten.
Hear=0 files converted, 3 kept as they were, 0 skipped for want of a conversion, 0 failed.

[step]
Say=Four: every run writes a log, with nothing to switch on, named at the end of the results.
Hear=The log: C colon backslash Users backslash you backslash AppData backslash Local backslash BatCon backslash logs backslash BatCon dash 20261020 dot log

[step]
Say=The guide and the hotkeys are in the help folder and on the project page. BatCon is one of the Homer Tools.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: the four things, and where help lives.
